ID: B2-Ch04b-Bastard
TEXT:

#if(v_b2_ch2_deal == 3) {
 "Wait, who are you, and what are you doing here?" Bruce says, finally noticing the lessathi in the dark blue robe.

"A late addition to your division," the lessathi says. "Taken in this morning."

"Tough luck," Bruce says. "Hope you know how to fight. This isn't a stroll."

"I will manage," the lessathi says.

A lion's roar rolls out from beyond the beast pens. Two manticores muscle their way past the iron grating, unfurling leathery wings before launching into the sky, circling high above the sand. Behind them march three desert marauders, their chitin plates scraping as they scuttle into the open. Two giant acid-spitting cobras slide from the shadows, hoods flared wide, and beneath the packed dirt, the heavy rhythm of hooves signals tramplers winding up for a charge.

"For this match, we have a special demonstration," the announcer's voice booms across the tiers through the magnifier. "The fourth division will face four distinct breeds of our deadliest beasts at once. Survival requires clearing the entire floor. A special arrangement, courtesy of our esteemed arena master, Lord Venard."

Venard. The petty tyrant wants to see if I can match Hadrik and Daren in a single heat.

"Form on me!" Bruce barks. "Follow my lead and we make it through!"

"Right on cue," the ex-noble thug sneers. "Ten seconds on the sand and you think you're captain. Shove your orders where the sun doesn't reach. Nobody's taking marching orders from you."

}
#if(v_b2_ch2_deal != 3) {
 A lion's roar rolls out from beyond the beast pens. Two manticores muscle their way past the iron grating, unfurling leathery wings before launching into the sky, circling high above the sand. Behind them march three desert marauders, their chitin plates scraping as they scuttle into the open. Two giant acid-spitting cobras slide from the shadows, hoods flared wide, and beneath the packed dirt, the heavy rhythm of hooves signals tramplers winding up for a charge.

"For this match, we have a special demonstration," the announcer's voice booms across the tiers through the magnifier. "The fourth division will face four distinct breeds of our deadliest beasts at once. Survival requires clearing the entire floor. A special arrangement, courtesy of our esteemed arena master, Lord Venard."

Venard. The petty tyrant wants to see if I can match Hadrik and Daren in a single heat.

"Form on me!" Bruce barks. "Follow my lead and we make it through!"

"Right on cue," the ex-noble thug sneers. "Ten seconds on the sand and you think you're captain. Shove your orders where the sun doesn't reach. Nobody's taking marching orders from you."

}
