ID: B2-Ch04b-Wilhelm-lessathi
TEXT:

#if(v_b2_ch2_lessathi == 1 && v_b2_ch2_threatened != 0 || v_b2_ch2_threatened == 1) {
 Wilhelm is no longer standing with the group. A familiar chill hits the back of my neck.

I pivot fast. Wilhelm stands two paces back, gripping an orange-hilted dagger in both hands, poised for a killing thrust.

"Something on your mind, Wilhelm?" I say.

He locks up mid-step. The blade stays raised, his knuckles white, but facing me directly, his assassin training forces hesitation over commitment.

"Put that away before you hurt yourself," I tell him.

Sweat beads on his brow. He holds my stare for three silent seconds, slides the blade into its sheath, and walks toward our holding pen without a word.

Good. Hopefully the message took.

}
#if(v_b2_ch2_fist == 1 && v_b2_ch2_threatened == 0 || v_b2_ch2_fist == 2 && v_b2_ch2_threatened == 0) {
 Wilhelm is gone from the group. The dust barely settled and he vanished. Then Bruce's warning clicks: assassin.

A bad feeling knots in my stomach. I spin on my heel. Wilhelm is right behind me, gripping an orange-hilted dagger in both hands, positioned to drive it between my shoulder blades.

"Something on your mind, Wilhelm?" I say.

He locks up mid-step. The blade stays raised, his knuckles white, but facing me directly, his assassin training forces hesitation over commitment.

"Put that away before you hurt yourself," I tell him.

Sweat beads on his brow. He holds my stare for three silent seconds, slides the blade into its sheath, and walks toward our holding pen without a word.

Good. Hopefully the message took.

}
#if(v_b2_ch2_threatened == 0 && v_b2_ch2_fist != 1 && v_b2_ch2_fist != 2) {
 Wilhelm is gone from the group. The fight just ended.

I turn to find him standing two paces behind me, gripping an orange-hilted dagger in both hands, poised to plunge it into my back.

"Wilhelm?" I say.

He freezes. The weapon stays raised, but he seems unable to drive the strike home.

"Wilhelm, what are you doing?" I ask.

Sweat glints on his forehead. He stands motionless under my gaze, then silently sheathes the blade and heads for our division pen.

What was that about?

}
choice("Continue", B2-Ch04b-Associates, v_current_scene = B2-Ch04b-Associates)


ID: B2-Ch04b-Associates
TEXT:

 "Ladies and gentlemen," the announcer calls out, straining against the wall of booing from the stands, "I share your confusion over this turn of events. While the situation is clear to the eye, our regulations require formal verification before confirming a breach, as our sensory arrays did not trigger. Until the review concludes, this participant remains in our custody. Thank you for your patience."

"Well," Bruce grunts. "First round's settled. Back to the pen."

At the division gate, the arena owner stands waiting, blocking the corridor.

"An explanation, if you please," the owner snaps, glaring at the lessathi. "Who gave you permission to disrupt my arena?"

"You know very well who did," the lessathi replies evenly. "Step aside and let me pass, if you know what is good for you."

"How did you bypass the magic detectors?" the owner demands.

"Who do you think supplied those devices in the first place?" the lessathi says. "A minor calibration before the match, and they ignore electrical discharge completely."

"You will not set foot in this arena again," the owner snarls. "Get out of here. Now!"

"Are you certain?" the lessathi asks, tone dropping to a sharp chill.

"Get out!"

"Very well. You will not see me again. You will, however, receive a visit from my associates in the coming days. When they arrive, prepare to answer for today."

The lessathi walks off without another word, and the owner retreats toward his box. The six of us file back into our division quarters, and the iron portcullis clangs shut. A quick glance around the chamber confirms Wilhelm is missing.

"Where do you suppose Wilhelm went?" Bruce asks.

"Who cares?" the thug grunts. "Long wait before the second round. He'll show up."

"Attention, please," the announcer's voice cuts in from above. "We require a brief recess to audit our creature pens. Remain in your seats! This will not take long!"

"Hah!" Bruce snorts. "They're running out of beasts already. Weren't counting on us clearing the pens so fast!"

choice(""Was that all? I was hoping to see a more impressive collection of creatures."", B2-Ch04b-Collection, v_current_scene = B2-Ch04b-Collection)
choice(""I don't think they're done. I haven't even seen any griffins, yet."", B2-Ch04b-Griffins, v_current_scene = B2-Ch04b-Griffins)
choice(""Or maybe they're only done with the small fry, and the show is just beginning."", B2-Ch04b-Fry, v_current_scene = B2-Ch04b-Fry)


ID: B2-Ch04b-Argument2
TEXT:

#if(v_b2_ch4_argument == 1) {
 "Is this really the time and place to be having this argument?"

"What's your plan, genius?" the thug sneers. "Kneel to the great and mighty Bruce and beg for orders?"

"No," I say. "I'm telling you to shut your mouth and watch the floor. They're already moving to flank us."

The cobras slide out wide to our right; the marauders scuttle along the left. Three tramplers paw the ground, heavy hooves digging furrows into the dirt as they line up a charge. Above us, manticores bank in wide circles, biding their time.

}
#if(v_b2_ch4_argument == 2) {
 "Actually, I think that Bruce would do just fine as leader."

"Think so?" the thug sneers. "Why don't the two of you march out there together? At least you'll buy the rest of us some time."

"Or you could shut your mouth and watch the floor," I say. "They're already moving to flank us."

The cobras slide out wide to our right; the marauders scuttle along the left. Three tramplers paw the ground, heavy hooves digging furrows into the dirt as they line up a charge. Above us, manticores bank in wide circles, biding their time.

}
#if(v_b2_ch4_argument == 3) {
 "I completely agree. I should be the one to lead the team, not Bruce."

"If you're so eager to take charge," the thug sneers, "go on ahead. We'll be right behind you. Promise."

"How about you shut your mouth and watch the floor," I say. "They're already moving to flank us."

The cobras slide out wide to our right; the marauders scuttle along the left. Three tramplers paw the ground, heavy hooves digging furrows into the dirt as they line up a charge. Above us, manticores bank in wide circles, biding their time.

}
choice("Charge at the creatures all by myself", B2-Ch04b-Charge, v_current_scene = B2-Ch04b-Charge, v_b2_ch4_charge = 1)
choice("Charge at the creatures and ask Leila to join me", B2-Ch04b-Charge, v_current_scene = B2-Ch04b-Charge, v_b2_ch4_charge = 2)
choice("Wait for the creatures to get further away from each other before attacking", B2-Ch04b-Further, v_current_scene = B2-Ch04b-Further, v_b2_ch4_charge = 3)


ID: B2-Ch04b-Charge
TEXT:

#if(v_b2_ch4_charge == 1) {
 Hadrik and Daren aren't the only ones who can take down monsters alone. If Venard wants a show, I'll give him one.

"I'm moving in," I say. "Wish me luck."

"You're what?" Bruce barks, caught flat-footed.

I break into a sprint across the sand. The pack has already begun to spread out, so I head for the desert marauders first—lowest immediate threat of the lot. I pick the scorpion-like beast trailing slightly behind the other two and close in for a thrust to its eyes.

}
#if(v_b2_ch4_charge == 2) {
 "I'm moving in," I say. "Leila, coming?"

"...What?" Leila's blue glyphs flash in the air. "Wait. We need to watch their movement first."

"I'm going ahead," I call over my shoulder. "Catch up if you change your mind."

I break into a sprint across the sand. The pack has already begun to spread out, so I head for the desert marauders first—lowest immediate threat of the lot. I pick the scorpion-like beast trailing slightly behind the other two and close in for a thrust to its eyes.

}
choice("Continue", B2-Ch04b-Speed, v_current_scene = B2-Ch04b-Speed) if (v_b2_ch2_heard == 1 && v_b2_ch4_charge == 1 || v_b2_ch2_heard == 1 && v_b2_ch4_charge == 2 || v_b2_ch4_backpack == 2 && v_b2_ch4_charge == 1 || v_b2_ch4_backpack == 2 && v_b2_ch4_charge == 2 || v_b2_ch4_backpack == 3 && v_b2_ch4_charge == 1 || v_b2_ch4_backpack == 3 && v_b2_ch4_charge == 2)
choice("Continue", B2-Ch04b-Specific, v_current_scene = B2-Ch04b-Specific) if (v_b2_ch4_charge == 1 && v_b2_ch2_heard != 1 && v_b2_ch4_backpack != 2 && v_b2_ch4_backpack != 3 || v_b2_ch4_charge == 2 && v_b2_ch2_heard != 1 && v_b2_ch4_backpack != 2 && v_b2_ch4_backpack != 3)


ID: B2-Ch04b-Speed
TEXT:

#if(v_agility < 3) {
 

If my lore holds, when a giant scorpion-like creature is rushed head-on without overwhelming numbers, its primary instinct is a tail strike rather than a claw block. That leaves the head exposed, provided I have the foot speed to slip the stinger.

I enter tail range and prepare to lunge, but realize a fraction of a second too late that my burst is too slow. I throw myself backward, the dripping stinger kissing the air inches from my chin.

Speed won't cut it. I have to break through with brute force.

To reach the head, I need to strip its defenses. I circle wide and target the heavy claws one by one, keeping well outside the tail's forward sweep.

}
#if(v_agility >= 3) {
 

If my lore holds, when a giant scorpion-like creature is rushed head-on without overwhelming numbers, its primary instinct is a tail strike rather than a claw block. That leaves the head exposed, provided I have the foot speed to slip the stinger.

I close into tail range. The instant the stinger whips forward, I accelerate into the pocket, ducking beneath the arc to sink my dagger straight into its primary cluster of eyes. The beast recoils with a shrill hiss. Before it recovers, I wrench the blade free and drive it down into the base of its skull, severing the cord.

It drops limp. I pull my dagger from the chitin shell and pivot toward the remaining two marauders, weighing the next target.

}
choice("Continue", B2-Ch04b-Marauder, v_current_scene = B2-Ch04b-Marauder) if (v_agility < 3)
choice("Continue", B2-Ch04b-Manticore, v_current_scene = B2-Ch04b-Manticore) if (v_agility >= 3)


ID: B2-Ch04b-Specific
TEXT:

 The marauder raises its arched tail, poised to strike, and I ease back a half-step. Without detailed lore on this specific breed, I have to rely on standard anatomy: head and eye clusters remain the most vulnerable points. But a direct approach means running into two crushing pincers before the stinger finishes the job. Speed alone won't open a path; I need enough raw force to dismantle its guard.

To clear a line to the head, I have to take out the claws first. I circle in, testing its reach while staying clear of the tail's forward sweep.

choice("Continue", B2-Ch04b-Marauder, v_current_scene = B2-Ch04b-Marauder)


ID: B2-Ch04b-Marauder
TEXT:

set(v_is_dead,0) if (v_reflexes >= 3 || v_strength >= 3)
set(v_is_dead,1) if (v_reflexes < 3 && v_strength < 3)
#if(v_strength >= 3) {
 

Daren's enchantment pays for itself. Cleaving through reinforced chitin in a single blow should be impossible, but the enchanted edge bites clean through the marauder's left pincer, shearing it off at the joint. With its primary guard broken, I slip past the severed side and drive straight for the head. The stinger lacks the lateral pivot to track me. I sink the dagger deep into its right eye cluster, then wrench it free and drive it down through the base of its skull.

The beast collapses into the sand. I pull my blade from the shell and turn toward the remaining two scorpions to pick the next target.

}
#if(v_reflexes >= 3 && v_strength < 3) {
 

Even with the enchanted blade, my strikes lack the weight to sever heavy chitin outright. After ten seconds of trading blows, the beast catches me off-balance and whips its tail straight for my chest.

Reflexes take over. My arm snaps up, parrying the stinger right above my brow with the flat of the dagger. As the tail recoils from the deflection, an opening clears. I surge forward before the claws can close, sinking the dagger into its right eye cluster, then driving the blade into the base of its skull.

The beast drops limp. I pull my blade from the shell and turn toward the remaining two scorpions to pick the next target.

}
#if(v_reflexes < 3 && v_strength < 3) {
 

Even with the enchanted blade, my strikes lack the weight to sever heavy chitin outright. After ten seconds of trading blows, the beast catches me off-balance and whips its tail straight for my chest.

My reaction is too slow. The barbed stinger punches clean through my skull before my blade can rise, and the world goes black.

}
choice("Continue", B2-Ch04b-Manticore, v_current_scene = B2-Ch04b-Manticore) if (v_reflexes >= 3 || v_strength >= 3)
choice("Restart game", Ch1-Intro1, v_current_scene = Ch1-Intro1, special:restart) if (v_reflexes < 3 && v_strength < 3)
choice("Load from last checkpoint", , v_chapter_save_counter = 5, special:checkpoint_load) if (v_reflexes < 3 && v_strength < 3)
choice("Load game", , , special:saves) if (v_reflexes < 3 && v_strength < 3)


ID: B2-Ch04b-Manticore
TEXT:

set(v_is_dead,0) if (v_b2_ch4_backpack == 2 && v_premonition >= 1 || v_b2_ch4_backpack == 2 && v_hearing >= 2 && v_reflexes >= 2 || v_b2_ch4_backpack == 1 || v_b2_ch4_backpack == 3)
set(v_is_dead,1) if (v_b2_ch4_backpack == 2 && v_hearing < 2 && v_premonition < 1 || v_b2_ch4_backpack == 2 && v_premonition < 1 && v_reflexes < 2)
#if(v_b2_ch4_backpack == 1 && v_premonition >= 1 || v_b2_ch4_backpack == 1 && v_reflexes >= 2 || v_b2_ch4_backpack == 1 && v_hearing < 2 || v_b2_ch4_backpack == 3 && v_premonition >= 1 || v_b2_ch4_backpack == 3 && v_reflexes >= 2 || v_b2_ch4_backpack == 3 && v_hearing < 2 || v_b2_ch4_backpack != 2) {
 Wait. The air shifts above me.

I glance up. A manticore is plummeting in a steep dive, talons flared. Exactly as anticipated—they hunt opportunistic kills right after a combatant engages, just like in Hadrik's bout.

I drop low, rolling across the sand, and lash out as it skims the dirt. The blade cuts deep across its primary wing joint, severing the flight feathers.

The beast screeches, flapping hard, but loses all lift and slams heavily into the sand. I close the distance before it can right itself, drawing the dagger across its throat in one clean motion.

}
#if(v_b2_ch4_backpack == 2 && v_premonition >= 1) {
 

A sudden flash hits my mind—a shadow dropping from above, talons sinking into bone.

I glance up to confirm, then spring backward. As the manticore stoops past my chest, I slash upward across its wing joint, shearing through the flight feathers.

The beast tries to bank, loses all lift, and crashes into the dirt. I cross the gap before it recovers, driving my blade through its throat to finish it.

}
#if(v_b2_ch4_backpack == 2 && v_hearing < 2 && v_premonition < 1) {
 

As I step toward the remaining marauders, a crushing weight slams into my back. Leathery wings beat against my ears as talons tear deep into my ribs. Before I can raise my blade, heavy fangs clamp onto the side of my neck, crushing my throat.

}
#if(v_b2_ch4_backpack == 2 && v_hearing >= 2 && v_reflexes >= 2 && v_premonition < 1) {
 

A sharp rush of wind cuts through the air directly above. I snap my head up: a manticore is dropping in a vertical dive, less than a heartbeat from tearing into my shoulders.

I throw myself sideways at the last possible fraction of a second, slashing upward into the beast's wing as it clears my head. The flight feathers shear clean off. The creature tumbles, unable to hold air, and skids hard across the sand. I lunge in before it finds its footing, drawing my dagger across its throat.

}
#if(v_b2_ch4_backpack == 2 && v_hearing >= 2 && v_premonition < 1 && v_reflexes < 2) {
 

A sharp rush of wind cuts through the air directly above. I snap my head up: a manticore is dropping in a vertical dive, less than a heartbeat from tearing into my shoulders.

I try to dive, but my feet are too slow. Talons punch through my chest, pinning me to the sand, and heavy fangs crush my neck before I can scream.

}
choice("Restart game", Ch1-Intro1, v_current_scene = Ch1-Intro1, special:restart) if (v_b2_ch4_backpack == 2 && v_hearing < 2 && v_premonition < 1 || v_b2_ch4_backpack == 2 && v_premonition < 1 && v_reflexes < 2)
