ID: B2-Ch04b-Wilhelm-charge
TEXT:

set(v_ac_b2_ch4_intimidation,1) if (v_b2_ch2_lessathi == 0 && v_b2_ch2_threatened == 2)
achievement("Intimidation successful",v_ac_b2_ch4_intimidation)
#if(v_b2_ch2_lessathi == 0 && v_b2_ch2_threatened == 2 && v_b2_ch4_charge == 1) {
 Two beasts down. What about Wilhelm? Is he making his move?

I glance back. Wilhelm is crouching behind a dead beast's shell, using the carcass as a shield against potential trampler charges. The threat from three days ago evidently worked.

Leila catches up, projecting blue letters in midair before she even halts.

"You could have asked me to come," the writing reads, her expression pinched in mild irritation.

"My mistake," I say as she pulls up. "Didn't think you wanted in."

"Which one first?" she writes.

"That marauder on the flank," I say, pointing toward the nearest scorpion.

}
#if(v_b2_ch2_lessathi == 0 && v_b2_ch2_threatened == 2 && v_b2_ch4_charge == 2) {
 Two beasts down. What about Wilhelm? Is he making his move?

I glance back. Wilhelm is crouching behind a dead beast's shell, using the carcass as a shield against potential trampler charges. The threat from three days ago evidently worked.

Leila catches up, projecting blue letters in midair.

"Changed my mind," the writing reads. "Here to help."

"Good," I say as she halts beside me. "Let's take that marauder on the flank first."

}
#if(v_b2_ch2_threatened == 1 && v_b2_ch4_charge == 1 || v_b2_ch2_lessathi == 1 && v_b2_ch4_charge == 1 && v_b2_ch2_threatened != 0) {
 Two beasts down. What about Wilhelm? Is he making his move?

I spin around. Wilhelm stands directly behind me, orange-hilted dagger raised in both hands, set to strike.

There he is.

Before I can step inside his reach, a shadow moves behind him. A heavy crack echoes as the butt of Leila's dagger catches him behind the ear. Wilhelm drops face-first onto the sand, out cold.

"You could have asked me to come," Leila writes, glaring at me with folded arms.

"My mistake," I say. "Didn't think you wanted in."

"Which one first?" she writes.

"That marauder over there," I say, nodding toward the nearest scorpion.

}
#if(v_b2_ch2_threatened == 1 && v_b2_ch4_charge == 2 || v_b2_ch2_lessathi == 1 && v_b2_ch4_charge == 2 && v_b2_ch2_threatened != 0) {
 Two beasts down. What about Wilhelm? Is he making his move?

I spin around. Wilhelm stands directly behind me, orange-hilted dagger raised in both hands, set to strike.

There he is.

Before I can step inside his reach, a shadow moves behind him. A heavy crack echoes as the butt of Leila's dagger catches him behind the ear. Wilhelm drops face-first onto the sand, out cold.

"Changed my mind," Leila writes. "Here to help."

"Good," I say. "Let's take that marauder over there first."

}
#if(v_b2_ch2_threatened == 0 && v_b2_ch4_charge == 1 && v_b2_ch2_fist != 1 && v_b2_ch2_fist != 2) {
 Two beasts down. Next target.

A dull thud hits the dirt behind me. I turn around. Wilhelm lies sprawled on the ground, unconscious, with Leila standing over him. An orange-hilted dagger rests in the sand near his limp fingers. Orange hilts are standard for assassins—enchanted to mask the wielder's aura. Was Wilhelm sent here to kill me?

"You could have asked me to come," Leila writes, looking irritated.

"What happened to Wilhelm?" I ask.

"Self-explanatory," she writes. "He tried to stab you. I stopped him."

"Damn," I mutter. "I barely know the man. No idea why he wants me dead."

"What's the plan?" she writes. "Which creature first?"

"That marauder over there," I say, pointing toward the nearest scorpion.

}
