choice("Continue", B2-Ch04b-Obstacles, v_current_scene = B2-Ch04b-Obstacles)


ID: B2-Ch04b-Obstacles
TEXT:

#if(v_b2_ch2_fist == 1 || v_b2_ch2_fist == 2) {
 Bruce jogs up to us, chest heaving as he plants his boots in the sand.

"You've both lost your minds!" Bruce pants.

"You followed us out here, so make room for a third," I tell him.

"What's the plan?" Bruce asks.

"We were about to take out the--"

I cut myself off. The cobras are slithering closer across the sand, while two tramplers wheel about, searching for an unobstructed line to launch a full charge.

"Scratch that," I say. "Give me a second to read the field."

}
#if(v_b2_ch2_fist != 1 && v_b2_ch2_fist != 2) {
 The cobras are slithering closer across the sand, while two tramplers wheel about, searching for an unobstructed line to launch a full charge.

"Scratch that," I say to Leila. "Give me a second to read the field."

}
choice("Try to bait the cobras into spitting acid on the marauders", B2-Ch04b-Lure, v_current_scene = B2-Ch04b-Lure, v_b2_ch4_tactic = 1)
choice("Ask Leila if she can deal with the tramplers, while we deal with the cobras", B2-Ch04b-Leila-tramplers, v_current_scene = B2-Ch04b-Leila-tramplers, v_b2_ch4_tactic = 2) if (v_b2_ch2_fist == 1 || v_b2_ch2_fist == 2)
choice("Focus on killing the manticore, first", B2-Ch04b-Manticore-first, v_current_scene = B2-Ch04b-Manticore-first, v_b2_ch4_tactic = 3)
choice("Ask Leila if she can deal with the tramplers, while I deal with the cobras", B2-Ch04b-Leila-tramplers, v_current_scene = B2-Ch04b-Leila-tramplers, v_b2_ch4_tactic = 2) if (v_b2_ch2_fist != 1 && v_b2_ch2_fist != 2)


ID: B2-Ch04b-Manticore-first
TEXT:

set(v_ac_b2_ch4_spear,1) if (v_combat_technique >= 1 && v_strength >= 1)
achievement("Spear thrower",v_ac_b2_ch4_spear)
#if(v_strength < 1 && v_b2_ch2_fist != 1 && v_b2_ch2_fist != 2) {
 

"We bring down that manticore first," I say. "Can't focus on ground targets with claws hanging over our heads."

"What's the play?" Leila writes.

"Spear volley," I tell her, gesturing toward the rack of weapons mounted along the arena perimeter.

"Move," Leila writes.

We skirt the marauder carcasses, tracking the tramplers and cobras as we sprint for the wall. I snatch a spear from the iron bracket, plant my feet, and hurl it toward the circling beast. The throw falls short, dipping into the sand well below the manticore's altitude.

That's what happens when you try to show off with zero spear training.

Leila exhales a quiet sigh.

"Move," she writes. "My turn."

She grips a spear, steps into the throw, and launches it. The shaft streaks across the sky, punching straight through the manticore's chest. The beast folds in midair and crashes into the dirt.

}
#if(v_b2_ch2_fist == 1 && v_strength < 1 || v_b2_ch2_fist == 2 && v_strength < 1) {
 

"We bring down that manticore first," I say. "Can't focus on ground targets with claws hanging over our heads."

"What's the play?" Leila writes.

"Spear volley," I tell her, gesturing toward the rack of weapons mounted along the arena perimeter.

"Move fast," Bruce grunts. "Those tramplers are lining up."

We skirt the marauder carcasses, tracking the tramplers and cobras as we sprint for the wall. I snatch a spear from the iron bracket, plant my feet, and hurl it toward the circling beast. The throw falls short, dipping into the sand well below the manticore's altitude.

That's what happens when you try to show off with zero spear training.

"Seriously?" Bruce says, rolling his eyes. "First time holding a shaft? Step aside and watch."

Bruce heaves a spear from the wall and launches it with full torso torque. The steel point buries itself deep in the manticore's chest, dropping it out of the sky in a heavy thud.

}
#if(v_strength >= 1 && v_combat_technique < 1 && v_b2_ch2_fist != 1 && v_b2_ch2_fist != 2) {
 

"We bring down that manticore first," I say. "Can't focus on ground targets with claws hanging over our heads."

"What's the play?" Leila writes.

"Spear volley," I tell her, gesturing toward the rack of weapons mounted along the arena perimeter.

"Move," Leila writes.

We skirt the marauder carcasses, tracking the tramplers and cobras as we sprint for the wall. I snatch a spear from the iron bracket, plant my feet, and hurl it with all the force in my arm. The distance is there, but the aim drifts wide. The shaft sails uselessly past the wing and clatters onto the sand.

Zero spear technique will do that.

Leila exhales a quiet sigh.

"Move," she writes. "My turn."

She takes a spear from the wall, steps into the motion, and releases. The spear punches straight through the manticore's chest, dropping it dead out of the sky.

}
#if(v_b2_ch2_fist == 1 && v_strength >= 1 && v_combat_technique < 1 || v_b2_ch2_fist == 2 && v_strength >= 1 && v_combat_technique < 1) {
 

"We bring down that manticore first," I say. "Can't focus on ground targets with claws hanging over our heads."

"What's the play?" Leila writes.

"Spear volley," I tell her, gesturing toward the rack of weapons mounted along the arena perimeter.

"Move fast," Bruce grunts. "Those tramplers are lining up."

We skirt the marauder carcasses, tracking the tramplers and cobras as we sprint for the wall. I snatch a spear from the iron bracket, plant my feet, and hurl it with all the force in my arm. The distance is there, but the aim drifts wide. The shaft sails uselessly past the wing and clatters onto the sand.

Zero spear technique will do that.

"Seriously?" Bruce says, shaking his head. "First time holding a shaft? Step aside and watch."

Bruce heaves a spear from the wall and launches it with full torso torque. The steel point buries itself deep in the manticore's chest, dropping it out of the sky in a heavy thud.

The stands roar. The crowd has been cheering for a while, but my focus has been locked on the sand.

With the flyer down, the tramplers complete their turn, squaring up for a full-tilt charge. The cobras slide toward us in lockstep. The scorpions have peeled off, scuttling toward the rest of the division.

}
#if(v_combat_technique >= 1 && v_strength >= 1 && v_b2_ch2_fist != 1 && v_b2_ch2_fist != 2) {
 

"We bring down that manticore first," I say. "Can't focus on ground targets with claws hanging over our heads."

"What's the play?" Leila writes.

"Spear volley," I tell her, gesturing toward the rack of weapons mounted along the arena perimeter.

"Move," Leila writes.

We skirt the marauder carcasses, tracking the tramplers and cobras as we sprint for the wall. I snatch a spear from the iron bracket, shift my weight, and let fly with clean form. The throw drives true. The iron point punches clean through the manticore's chest, killing it in mid-flight and sending the carcass crashing into the dirt.

}
#if(v_b2_ch2_fist == 1 && v_combat_technique >= 1 && v_strength >= 1 || v_b2_ch2_fist == 2 && v_combat_technique >= 1 && v_strength >= 1) {
 

"We bring down that manticore first," I say. "Can't focus on ground targets with claws hanging over our heads."

"What's the play?" Leila writes.

"Spear volley," I tell her, gesturing toward the rack of weapons mounted along the arena perimeter.

"Move fast," Bruce grunts. "Those tramplers are lining up."

We skirt the marauder carcasses, tracking the tramplers and cobras as we sprint for the wall. I snatch a spear from the iron bracket, shift my weight, and let fly with clean form. The throw drives true. The iron point punches clean through the manticore's chest, killing it in mid-flight and sending the carcass crashing into the dirt.

}
#if(v_b2_ch2_fist != 1 && v_b2_ch2_fist != 2 || v_combat_technique >= 1 || v_strength < 1) {
 The stands roar. The crowd has been cheering for a while, but my focus has been locked on the sand.

With the flyer down, the tramplers complete their turn, squaring up for a full-tilt charge. The cobras slide toward us in lockstep. The scorpions have peeled off, scuttling toward the rest of the division.

}
choice("Continue", B2-Ch04b-Strength-check, v_current_scene = B2-Ch04b-Strength-check)


ID: B2-Ch04b-Strength-check
TEXT:

#if(v_strength < 2) {
 

"Leila," I say. "Take the tramplers. With your enhanced strength, you can pierce their hide. I'll tie up the cobras."

"On it," Leila writes.

"Remember the weak points?" I ask.

"Understood," she writes, already sprinting toward the tramplers.

}
#if(v_strength >= 2 && v_b2_ch2_fist != 1 && v_b2_ch2_fist != 2) {
 

"Leila, take the cobras," I say. "I'll handle the tramplers. My strength stat should punch through their hide."

"On it," Leila writes.

"Remember the weak points?" I ask.

"Understood," she writes, turning toward the serpents.

As Leila splits off, I jog out to meet the tramplers.

}
#if(v_b2_ch2_fist == 1 && v_strength >= 2 || v_b2_ch2_fist == 2 && v_strength >= 2) {
 

"Leila, take the cobras," I say. "I'll handle the tramplers. My strength stat should punch through their hide."

"On it," Leila writes.

"Remember the weak points?" I ask.

"Understood," she writes.

"Bruce, go with her," I add. "I don't think your blade cuts through trampler armor."

"Right," Bruce grunts. "Moving."

As the two of them peel off, I jog out to meet the tramplers.

}
choice("Continue", B2-Ch04b-Cobras, v_current_scene = B2-Ch04b-Cobras) if (v_strength < 2)
choice("Continue", B2-Ch04b-Barry-tramplers, v_current_scene = B2-Ch04b-Barry-tramplers) if (v_strength >= 2)


ID: B2-Ch04b-Cobras
TEXT:

#if(v_b2_ch4_tactic == 3 && v_b2_ch2_fist != 1 && v_b2_ch2_fist != 2) {
 I close the distance on the cobras. Seeing me approach, both serpents coil and raise their hoods.

Lore check: cobras need a solid two seconds to track and compress their venom glands. Constant lateral movement prevents them from locking on. But dodging alone won't create an opening; I have to bait the shot.

I plant my boots and hold dead still for two counts, then dive sideways the instant their throats contract. Twin jets of sizzling acid hiss through empty air and scorch the sand. While their venom glands refill, I lunge inside the right cobra's reach, driving my dagger through its skull. The second serpent lunges to snap my head off, but the wind-up teases its trajectory—I side-step the strike and draw my blade across its neck as it passes.

I check on Leila. She has already dispatched both tramplers and is jogging back.

What about the marauders?

}
#if(v_b2_ch4_tactic == 2 && v_b2_ch2_fist != 1 && v_b2_ch2_fist != 2) {
 I close the distance on the cobras. Seeing me approach, both serpents coil and raise their hoods.

Lore check: cobras need a solid two seconds to track and compress their venom glands. Constant lateral movement prevents them from locking on. But dodging alone won't create an opening; I have to bait the shot.

I plant my boots and hold dead still for two counts, then dive sideways the instant their throats contract. Twin jets of sizzling acid hiss through empty air and scorch the sand. While their venom glands refill, I lunge inside the right cobra's reach, driving my dagger through its skull. The second serpent lunges to snap my head off, but the wind-up teases its trajectory—I side-step the strike and draw my blade across its neck as it passes.

I check on Leila. She has already dispatched both tramplers and is jogging back. She also dropped the second manticore.

What about the marauders? Last I checked, they were bearing down on the rest of the team.

}
#if(v_b2_ch4_tactic == 1 && v_b2_ch2_fist != 1 && v_b2_ch2_fist != 2) {
 I close the distance on the cobras. Seeing me approach, both serpents coil and raise their hoods.

Lore check: cobras need a solid two seconds to track and compress their venom glands. Constant lateral movement prevents them from locking on. But dodging alone won't create an opening; I have to bait the shot.

I plant my boots and hold dead still for two counts, then dive sideways the instant their throats contract. Twin jets of sizzling acid hiss through empty air and scorch the sand. While their venom glands refill, I lunge inside the right cobra's reach, driving my dagger through its skull. The second serpent lunges to snap my head off, but the wind-up teases its trajectory—I side-step the strike and draw my blade across its neck as it passes.

I check on Leila. She has already dispatched both tramplers and is jogging back.

That's the round. We cleared the floor. The stands are in an uproar—they clearly expected a bloodbath. If Hadrik were here, he'd probably give a grand victory speech, but all I want is to get back into the pen and rest before the next heat.

After a moment, the announcer calls for the floor to be cleared, and we turn toward the division gate.

}
#if(v_b2_ch2_fist == 1 || v_b2_ch2_fist == 2) {
 "Bruce, stay with me," I say. "I don't think your blade punches through trampler hide."

"Understood," Bruce says. "Right behind you."

We move toward the cobras, which coil and raise their flared hoods.

"Keep moving laterally," I tell Bruce. "They spit in a straight line and need two seconds to lock on. Don't give them a static target."

"Got it," Bruce says.

"Take the left one," I say, sprinting for the right.

}
#if(v_b2_ch2_fist == 1 && v_b2_ch4_tactic == 3 || v_b2_ch2_fist == 2 && v_b2_ch4_tactic == 3) {
 I stand still for two counts, baiting the spit, then dive clear. Acid hisses harmlessly into the dirt. While the glands reload, I surge forward and drive my blade into the snake's skull.

I check Bruce. He handled his side cleanly—the other cobra lies headless on the sand, and Bruce is walking over, broadsword resting on his shoulder. Leila has finished the tramplers and is heading our way.

What about the marauders?

}
#if(v_b2_ch2_fist == 1 && v_b2_ch4_tactic == 2 || v_b2_ch2_fist == 2 && v_b2_ch4_tactic == 2) {
 I stand still for two counts, baiting the spit, then dive clear. Acid hisses harmlessly into the dirt. While the glands reload, I surge forward and drive my blade into the snake's skull.

I check Bruce. He handled his side cleanly—the other cobra lies headless on the sand, and Bruce is walking over, broadsword resting on his shoulder. Leila has finished the tramplers and is heading our way. She has the second manticore down as well.

What about the marauders? Last I checked, they were bearing down on the rest of the team.

}
#if(v_b2_ch2_fist == 1 && v_b2_ch4_tactic == 1 || v_b2_ch2_fist == 2 && v_b2_ch4_tactic == 1) {
 I stand still for two counts, baiting the spit, then dive clear. Acid hisses harmlessly into the dirt. While the glands reload, I surge forward and drive my blade into the snake's skull.

I check Bruce. He handled his side cleanly—the other cobra lies headless on the sand, and Bruce is walking over, broadsword resting on his shoulder. Leila has finished the tramplers and is heading our way.

That's the round. We cleared the floor. The stands are in an uproar—they clearly expected a bloodbath. If Hadrik were here, he'd probably give a grand victory speech, but all I want is to get back into the pen and rest before the next heat.

After a moment, the announcer calls for the floor to be cleared, and we turn toward the division gate.

}
choice("Continue", B2-Ch04b-Signal, v_current_scene = B2-Ch04b-Signal) if (v_b2_ch4_tactic == 2 || v_b2_ch4_tactic == 3)
choice("Continue", B2-Ch04b-Wilhelm-final, v_current_scene = B2-Ch04b-Wilhelm-final) if (v_b2_ch4_tactic == 1)


ID: B2-Ch04b-Leila-tramplers
TEXT:

 "Leila," I say. "Take the tramplers. With your enhanced strength, you can break through their armor. I'll handle the cobras."

"On it," Leila writes.

"Remember the weak points?"

"Understood," she writes.

"One more thing," I add as she turns. "The manticore above will probably dive the moment a trampler drops. It saw its partner die when it came after me, so it won't pick me again. Watch the sky and take it down on the entry dive, or we'll be chasing it all day."

"Got it," she writes, and sprints for the tramplers.

choice("Continue", B2-Ch04b-Cobras, v_current_scene = B2-Ch04b-Cobras)


ID: B2-Ch04b-Lure
TEXT:

#if(v_b2_ch2_fist != 1 && v_b2_ch2_fist != 2) {
 "I have a plan," I say. "We do this together."

Leila nods.

"We bait the cobras over to the marauders," I say. "Stand with our backs to the scorpions. When the snakes spit, we dive out of the path and let the acid hit the marauders. Even if it doesn't kill them outright, it'll dissolve the chitin enough to finish them."

"Risky," Leila writes. "Mistime it, and we take acid to the chest or a stinger through the spine."

"Time it right, and we clear three threats in one move."

"Which three?" Leila writes. "Only two marauders left."

"The manticore above will dive the instant the marauders drop," I say. "It saw its partner die against me, so it'll target you. Be ready when it stoops."

"Understood," Leila writes. "I'll be ready."

"Move," I say.

We jog toward the cobras, hurling stones and shouting to pull their focus. Once locked onto us, we backtrack toward the marauders, pacing ourselves so the serpents follow without closing to strike range. We back right up against the marauders and hold position.

Those two seconds stretch thin. The cobras coil, throats swelling, and unleash twin streams of venom. We dive in opposite directions. The acid splashes square across the marauders' faces, sizzling through chitin. As the beasts thrash in pain, we dart in and sink our blades through their skulls.

Right on schedule, the remaining manticore folds its wings in a steep dive for Leila. She holds still until the shadow sweeps over her, then pivots and delivers a clean upward slash through its chest. The beast crashes hard, and she finishes it with a swift strike to the neck. We back away from the cobras while their glands regenerate.

Only the cobras and tramplers remain. The snakes are coiling for another volley, while the tramplers line up their charge across open sand.

}
#if(v_b2_ch2_fist == 1 || v_b2_ch2_fist == 2) {
