"Understood," Leila writes. "I'll be ready."

"Good plan," Bruce grunts. "Let's draw them in."

We jog toward the cobras, hurling stones and shouting to pull their focus. Once locked onto us, we backtrack toward the marauders, pacing ourselves so the serpents follow without closing to strike range. We back right up against the marauders and hold position.

