}
#if(v_b2_ch2_fist != 1 && v_b2_ch2_fist != 2 && v_b2_ch4_tactic != 1) {
 I duck beneath the swinging mace tail, slip to the right flank, and sink my dagger deep into the neck joint. The beast drops. I pivot instantly to the second trampler as it lowers its horns, step inside the thrust, and open its throat. It crashes to the sand, blood pooling beneath its snout.

Not bad.

I turn to check Leila. Both cobras are dead, and she is jogging toward me.

What about the marauders?

}
#if(v_b2_ch2_fist == 1 && v_b2_ch4_tactic != 1 || v_b2_ch2_fist == 2 && v_b2_ch4_tactic != 1) {
