Not bad.

I turn to check Leila. Both cobras are dead, and she is jogging toward me.

That's the round. We cleared the floor. The stands are in an uproar—they clearly expected a bloodbath. If Hadrik were here, he'd probably give a grand victory speech, but all I want is to get back into the pen and rest before the next heat.

After a moment, the announcer calls for the floor to be cleared, and we turn toward the division gate.

}
