ID: B2-Ch04b-Signal
TEXT:

set(v_ac_b2_ch4_player,1) if (v_b2_ch2_fist == 1 && v_b2_ch2_heard == 0 || v_b2_ch2_fist == 2 && v_b2_ch2_heard == 0 || v_b2_ch2_fist == 1 && v_b2_ch4_inform2 == 0 && v_b2_ch4_inform3 == 0 || v_b2_ch2_fist == 2 && v_b2_ch4_inform2 == 0 && v_b2_ch4_inform3 == 0)
achievement("Not a team player",v_ac_b2_ch4_player)
#if(v_b2_ch2_heard == 1 && v_b2_ch4_inform2 == 1 && v_b2_ch2_fist != 1 && v_b2_ch2_fist != 2 || v_b2_ch2_heard == 1 && v_b2_ch4_inform3 == 1 && v_b2_ch2_fist != 1 && v_b2_ch2_fist != 2) {
 I look toward the rest of the division. Surprisingly, all of them are still on their feet, and they have managed to bring down one of the marauders on their own. I signal Leila and we jog over.

Finishing off the final scorpion takes seconds. We don't even need specific weak points—four blades overwhelm its guard.

As we stand among the carcasses, a deafening cheer rolls down from the stands. The crowd never expected the fourth division to survive the opening heat. Bruce hoists his broadsword high in salute, but the rest of us just wait for the horn to clear the sand.

After a brief delay, the announcer calls the match, and we turn back toward our pen.

}
#if(v_b2_ch2_fist == 1 && v_b2_ch2_heard == 1 && v_b2_ch4_inform2 == 1 || v_b2_ch2_fist == 1 && v_b2_ch2_heard == 1 && v_b2_ch4_inform3 == 1 || v_b2_ch2_fist == 2 && v_b2_ch2_heard == 1 && v_b2_ch4_inform2 == 1 || v_b2_ch2_fist == 2 && v_b2_ch2_heard == 1 && v_b2_ch4_inform3 == 1) {
 I look toward the rest of the division. Surprisingly, all of them are still on their feet, and they have managed to bring down one of the marauders on their own. I signal Leila and Bruce, and we jog over.

Finishing off the final scorpion takes seconds. We don't even need specific weak points—four blades overwhelm its guard.

As we stand among the carcasses, a deafening cheer rolls down from the stands. The crowd never expected the fourth division to survive the opening heat. Bruce hoists his broadsword high in salute, but the rest of us just wait for the horn to clear the sand.

After a brief delay, the announcer calls the match, and we turn back toward our pen.

}
#if(v_b2_ch2_heard == 0 && v_b2_ch2_fist != 1 && v_b2_ch2_fist != 2 || v_b2_ch4_inform2 == 0 && v_b2_ch4_inform3 == 0 && v_b2_ch2_fist != 1 && v_b2_ch2_fist != 2) {
 I check the rest of the division. They aren't faring nearly as well. The ex-noble's companion lies motionless in the sand, and while they managed to kill one marauder, the second has them pinned against the wall.

I signal Leila and we sprint to reinforce them. Flanked on both sides, the scorpion goes down under a flurry of strikes.

A roar of applause rises from the arena tiers as the heat winds down. After a moment, the announcer calls for the floor to be cleared. We leave the dead thug on the sand and head for our division gate.

}
#if(v_b2_ch2_fist == 1 && v_b2_ch2_heard == 0 || v_b2_ch2_fist == 2 && v_b2_ch2_heard == 0 || v_b2_ch2_fist == 1 && v_b2_ch4_inform2 == 0 && v_b2_ch4_inform3 == 0 || v_b2_ch2_fist == 2 && v_b2_ch4_inform2 == 0 && v_b2_ch4_inform3 == 0) {
 I check the rest of the division. Both thugs lie dead in the sand. They managed to take down one marauder before falling, but the surviving scorpion is running the mage in circles, and he has zero room to mount a counterattack.

I signal Leila and Bruce, and the three of us intercept the beast. Triangulated and outnumbered, the marauder drops in seconds.

The crowd erupts into a thunderous roar. After a moment, the announcer calls the match. We leave the bodies behind and file into the tunnel.

}
choice("Continue", B2-Ch04b-Wilhelm-final, v_current_scene = B2-Ch04b-Wilhelm-final)


ID: B2-Ch04b-Further
TEXT:

 "Everyone, hide behind the monster carcasses!" Bruce says. "That way, the tramplers won't be able to charge at us."

"Well, what do you know!" Wilhelm says. "The brute can actually say some sensible things every once in a while!"

We duck behind a fallen marauder, scanning the dirt. The tramplers pace out wide, searching for an angle to charge without crashing into obstacles. The cobras and surviving marauders have spread across the flanks, and overhead, manticores bank in patient circles.

"If we stay huddled here, we're boxed in!" the thug's friend snarls. "We hit one group now while they're separated!"

"Charging blindly invites the tramplers to spear us!" the mage protests. "We hold the cover we have!"

"There's enough debris between here and the marauders to cover an advance," I say. "Short bounds from carcass to carcass until we close the distance. Keep a dead beast between our line and the tramplers, and their charge is neutralized."

#if(v_b2_ch4_backpack == 1) {
 "That... doesn't sound like a bad idea, actually," the mage says.

"Yes," Wilhelm says. "And if we travel as a group, we'll increase our chances of survival."

"Then let's get going," Bruce says. "And remember to keep a look out for the manticores in the sky. There's no telling when they'll take a dive for us."

We advance toward the desert marauders in coordinated bounds, halting behind carcasses to keep the tramplers' line of sight blocked. Once in position, we square up and engage.

}
#if(v_b2_ch4_backpack != 1) {
 "That... doesn't sound like a bad idea, actually," the mage says.

"Yes," Wilhelm says. "And if we travel as a group, we'll increase our chances of survival."

"Then let's get going," Bruce says. "And remember to keep a look out for the manticores in the sky. There's no telling when they'll take a dive for us."

We advance toward the desert marauders in coordinated bounds, halting behind carcasses to keep the tramplers' line of sight blocked. Between bounds, I run everyone through a quick briefing on marauder attack patterns and weak points so the whole squad strikes the right marks. Once in position, we square up and engage.

}
choice("Continue", B2-Ch04b-Woman, v_current_scene = B2-Ch04b-Woman)


ID: B2-Ch04b-Woman
TEXT:

#if(v_b2_ch2_heard == 0 && v_b2_ch4_backpack == 1) {
 Bruce initiates contact, roaring as he sweeps his heavy two-handed broadsword in wide arcs to intimidate the beasts. Leila darts for the nearest marauder's flank, probing for a line to its head, but the scorpion snaps its pincers and whips its tail across her line. She slips the blow and circles wide.

The second marauder charges the ex-noble thug, stinger raised to impale him. The thug stumbles back with a yelp, caught flat-footed. Before the barb lands, Bruce lunges across the dirt, parrying the stinger with the flat of his blade. The creature recoils, re-evaluating its opponent.

"The arena is no place for cowards!" Bruce shouts at the thug. "This is a place for real men! If you're planning to fight like a woman, then get out of my way!"

Bruce quickly catches the poor phrasing, glancing awkwardly toward Leila, who fixes him with a cold frown.

"Or you can... also fight like a woman if you want..." Bruce says. "Just don't be a coward. You get what I mean."

Bruce and Leila resume their fight with the front-line marauder, while Wilhelm provides support.
  
"Hey, you," I say. "Ex-noble thug!"

"What did you just call me?" the thug says, in a menacing tone.

"Never mind that!" I tell him. "Can you and your thug friend stand over here, and make some loud noises? I need someone to distract that marauder, so I can get behind it. The creature already took a liking to you, so you'd make the perfect distraction!"

"Screw you and your distractions!" the thug says. "Do you take me for a fool?"

"If it's just a distraction, then I can handle it," the mage says. "Where do you want me to stand?"

"Over there would be perfect," I tell him, as I point him in the right direction.

The two thugs peel off to join the others. The mage gets into position, pelting the marauder with stones to draw its focus. As soon as the beast turns toward him, I slip behind it and quickly scramble onto its back.

Without knowing its precise weak spot, the vulnerable area should sit somewhere along the upper dorsal plates. I test the joints between its scales with rapid, measured stabs to find the nerve cluster by process of elimination.

}
#if(v_b2_ch2_heard == 1 || v_b2_ch4_backpack != 1) {
 Bruce initiates contact, roaring as he sweeps his heavy two-handed broadsword in wide arcs to intimidate the beasts. Leila darts for the nearest marauder's flank, probing for a line to its head, but the scorpion snaps its pincers and whips its tail across her line. She slips the blow and circles wide.

The second marauder charges the ex-noble thug, stinger raised to impale him. The thug stumbles back with a yelp, caught flat-footed. Before the barb lands, Bruce lunges across the dirt, parrying the stinger with the flat of his blade. The creature recoils, re-evaluating its opponent.

"The arena is no place for cowards!" Bruce shouts at the thug. "This is a place for real men! If you're planning to fight like a woman, then get out of my way!"

Bruce quickly catches the poor phrasing, glancing awkwardly toward Leila, who fixes him with a cold frown.

"Or you can... also fight like a woman if you want..." Bruce says. "Just don't be a coward. You get what I mean."

Bruce and Leila resume their fight with the front-line marauder, while Wilhelm provides support.
  
"Hey, you," I say. "Ex-noble thug!"

"What did you just call me?" the thug says, in a menacing tone.

"Never mind that!" I tell him. "Can you and your thug friend stand over here, and make some loud noises? I need someone to distract that marauder, so I can get behind it. The creature already took a liking to you, so you'd make the perfect distraction!"

"Screw you and your distractions!" the thug says. "Do you take me for a fool?"

"If it's just a distraction, then I can handle it," the mage says. "Where do you want me to stand?"

"Over there would be perfect," I tell him, as I point him in the right direction.

The two thugs peel off to join the others. The mage gets into position, pelting the marauder with stones to draw its focus. As soon as the beast turns toward him, I slip behind it and quickly scramble onto its back.

Lore check: the dorsal weak spot on giant scorpions sits right between the upper back plates.

I drive the enchanted dagger straight between the two central scales. The marauder shrieks, thrashing violently as its nervous system misfires. The moment its legs give out and it crashes to the sand, I scramble forward and drive the blade into its skull. I drop off the carcass, dagger in hand, and get ready to join the team.

}
choice("Continue", B2-Ch04b-Marauder2, v_current_scene = B2-Ch04b-Marauder2) if (v_b2_ch2_heard == 0 && v_b2_ch4_backpack == 1)
choice("Continue", B2-Ch04b-Manticore, v_current_scene = B2-Ch04b-Manticore) if (v_b2_ch2_heard == 1 || v_b2_ch4_backpack != 1)


ID: B2-Ch04b-Marauder2
TEXT:

set(v_is_dead,0) if (v_reflexes >= 3 || v_strength >= 3)
set(v_is_dead,1) if (v_reflexes < 3 && v_strength < 3)
#if(v_strength >= 3) {
 

Testing the plates is a waste of time. With Daren's enchantment and my enhanced strength, brute force solves the problem.

I brace my boots against the carapace, grip the hilt with both hands, and strike hard at one of the dorsal scales. The chitin shatters under the blow. The blade punches deep into the creature's core, eliciting a shrill shriek as the beast thrashes and buckles. When it hits the sand, I slide forward and finish it with a clean thrust through the skull. I drop off the dead shell and scan the floor.

}
#if(v_reflexes >= 3 && v_strength < 3) {
 

As I probe for the joint, the marauder senses the weight on its back. It coils hard, arching its massive tail over its own head in a desperate, blinding strike meant to impale me where I crouch.

A beat of pure adrenaline—I see the barbed tip descending straight for my chest.

I throw my torso flat against its carapace, then roll sideways off its flank. The stinger drives downward with all the beast's momentum, too fast and too committed to brake. The heavy barb punches clean through its own dorsal plate, sinking deep into its spinal cluster and dumping a full payload of venom directly into its own nervous system.

The creature convulses violently, legs curling inward as the neurotoxin locks its body. Within seconds, the tremors stop, and the carcass lies dead in the sand. I scramble back to my feet and wipe the grit from my blade.

}
#if(v_reflexes < 3 && v_strength < 3) {
 

As I probe for the joint, the marauder senses the weight on its back. It coils hard, arching its massive tail over its own head in a desperate, blinding strike meant to impale me where I crouch.

I try to roll clear, but my reflexes lag. The barbed stinger punches straight through my chest, driving me into the sand. The venom hits like liquid fire, and my vision fades to black before I can draw breath.

}
choice("Continue", B2-Ch04b-Manticore, v_current_scene = B2-Ch04b-Manticore) if (v_reflexes >= 3 || v_strength >= 3)
choice("Restart game", Ch1-Intro1, v_current_scene = Ch1-Intro1, special:restart) if (v_reflexes < 3 && v_strength < 3)
choice("Load from last checkpoint", , v_chapter_save_counter = 5, special:checkpoint_load) if (v_reflexes < 3 && v_strength < 3)
choice("Load game", , , special:saves) if (v_reflexes < 3 && v_strength < 3)


ID: B2-Ch04b-Wilhelm-team
TEXT:

set(v_ac_b2_ch4_intimidation,1) if (v_b2_ch2_lessathi == 0 && v_b2_ch2_threatened == 2)
achievement("Intimidation successful",v_ac_b2_ch4_intimidation)
#if(v_b2_ch2_lessathi == 0 && v_b2_ch2_threatened == 2) {
 Two beasts down. What about Wilhelm? Is he making a move?

I turn around. Wilhelm is still engaged alongside the others, keeping his distance. The warning from three days ago clearly stuck.

I signal the mage, and we start heading towards the other marauders.

}
#if(v_b2_ch2_lessathi == 1 && v_b2_ch2_threatened != 0 || v_b2_ch2_cell == 1 && v_b2_ch2_lessathi == 1 && v_b2_ch2_threatened == 2 || v_b2_ch2_lessathi == 1 && v_b2_ch2_threatened == 2 && v_b2_ch2_fist != 1 && v_b2_ch2_fist != 2 || v_b2_ch2_threatened == 1) {
 Two beasts down. But a different problem looms.

Ever since stepping onto the sand, I've kept a corner of my eye on Wilhelm—my premonition never gave me a timestamp for his strike. I've tracked him drifting closer during the fight. Now he is gone from my peripheral vision. That means only one thing.

I pivot fast. Wilhelm stands two paces back, gripping his orange-hilted dagger in both hands, poised for a killing thrust.

With my eyes locked on his, he freezes. The assassin instincts in him scream to retreat when an ambush is spotted head-on.

"Wilhelm?" I say.

He stays silent, knuckles white on the hilt as sweat drips from his temple.

"Wilhelm, are you alright, my friend?" I tell him, with a concerned tone, as I put my left hand on his shoulder. "You look rather tense!"

}
#if(v_b2_ch2_threatened == 0 && v_b2_ch2_cell != 1 && v_b2_ch2_fist != 1 && v_b2_ch2_fist != 2) {
 Two beasts down. Next target.

A dull thud sounds behind me. I turn to see Wilhelm sprawled on the sand, out cold, with the mage standing over him. An orange-hilted dagger lies beside Wilhelm's limp fingers.

Orange hilts are standard for assassins—enchanted to mask the wielder's aura. Was Wilhelm hired to take me out?

No time to dissect it now. I'll figure it out after the horn.

"Why did you save me?" I ask the mage.

"I saved you," the mage says, "because I owed the silver haired princess for the advice that she gave me yesterday, about my device. With this, I'll consider my debt settled."

"I see," I say.

"Do you have any idea why mister smiley over here would want you dead?" the mage says.

"I don't know," I say. "But I don't want to waste time figuring that out now, in the middle of the battle. We're done here. Let's go help the others."

}
#if(v_b2_ch2_fist == 1 && v_b2_ch2_threatened == 0 && v_b2_ch2_cell != 1 || v_b2_ch2_fist == 2 && v_b2_ch2_threatened == 0 && v_b2_ch2_cell != 1) {
 Two beasts down. Next target.

A dull thud sounds behind me. I turn to see Wilhelm sprawled on the sand, out cold, with the mage standing over him. An orange-hilted dagger lies beside Wilhelm's limp fingers.

Why would Wilhelm want me dead? Bruce warned me he was an assassin, but targeting a random division-mate in the middle of a beast heat makes zero sense. Was there a contract on my head?

No time to dissect it now. I'll figure it out after the horn.

"Why did you save me?" I ask the mage.

"I saved you," the mage says, "because I owed the silver haired princess for the advice that she gave me yesterday, about my device. With this, I'll consider my debt settled."

"I see," I say.

"Do you have any idea why mister smiley over here would want you dead?" the mage says.

"I don't know," I say. "But I don't want to waste time figuring that out now, in the middle of the battle. We're done here. Let's go help the others."

}
#if(v_b2_ch2_lessathi == 1 && v_b2_ch2_threatened == 2 || v_b2_ch2_threatened == 1) {
 Before he can answer, I snap the pommel of my dagger hard into his left temple. His eyes roll back, and he collapses into the dirt, the orange-hilted blade tumbling from his grip.

"Idiot," I say to him, and then I begin heading towards the others.

"So, uh..." the mage's voice comes from behind as he jogs up. "Do you have any idea why mister smiley over there would want you dead?"

I'd forgotten the mage was right behind us.

"No idea," I say. "I'll figure it out later. Right now, we need to focus on killing the creatures."

}
choice("Continue", B2-Ch04b-Insane, v_current_scene = B2-Ch04b-Insane)


ID: B2-Ch04b-Wilhelm-checks
TEXT:

set(v_is_dead,0) if (v_hearing >= 1 && v_reflexes >= 1 || v_perception >= 1 && v_reflexes >= 1)
set(v_is_dead,1) if (v_hearing < 1 && v_perception < 1 || v_reflexes < 1)
#if(v_perception >= 1 && v_reflexes >= 1) {
 

I glance back toward Bruce and Leila and notice Wilhelm is missing from their line. I tracked him drifting toward my flank earlier while I was engaging the marauder. Where is he now?

A prickle of warning shoots down my neck. I spin.

The steel of an orange-hilted dagger is already closing on my chest.

I twist out of the line of the blade, step inside his guard, and drive the pommel of my dagger hard into his left temple. Wilhelm's eyes roll back, and he collapses into the sand, the weapon slipping from his limp fingers.

The attacker was Wilhelm.

}
