choice("Continue", B2-Ch04b-Over, v_current_scene = B2-Ch04b-Over)


ID: B2-Ch04b-Over
TEXT:

 "Make sure you never stop moving sideways," I tell Bruce, as we approach the snakes. "The cobras can only shoot their acid in a straight line, and it takes them a few seconds to take aim, so as long as you don't give them the time they need, they won't be able to hit you."

"Understood," Bruce says.

"You take the one on the left," I tell him, and I make a rush towards the cobra on the right.

I bait the cobra by standing in one place for two seconds, and then I jump out of the way, making the creature miss its shot, and waste its acid. While the snake is busy gathering up more acid in its glands, I make a dash towards it, and I stab it in the head, killing it in one strike. 

#if(v_b2_ch4_backup == 0) {
 I check Bruce. He handled his target cleanly—the headless cobra lies in the dirt, and Bruce is walking over, broadsword resting on his shoulder. Leila has cleared the tramplers and is heading our way, with the second manticore down as well.

That's the round. We cleared the floor. The stands are in an uproar—they clearly expected a bloodbath. If Hadrik were here, he'd probably give a grand victory speech, but all I want is to get back into the pen and rest before the next heat.

After a moment, the announcer calls for the floor to be cleared, and we turn toward the division gate.

}
#if(v_b2_ch4_backup == 1) {
 I check Bruce. He handled his target cleanly—the headless cobra lies in the dirt, and Bruce is walking over, broadsword resting on his shoulder, while Leila jogs up to join us.

That's the round. We cleared the floor. The stands are in an uproar—they clearly expected a bloodbath. If Hadrik were here, he'd probably give a grand victory speech, but all I want is to get back into the pen and rest before the next heat.

After a moment, the announcer calls for the floor to be cleared, and we turn toward the division gate.

}
choice("Continue", B2-Ch04b-Wilhelm-final, v_current_scene = B2-Ch04b-Wilhelm-final)


ID: B2-Ch04b-Wilhelm-final
TEXT:

set(v_ac_b2_ch4_stats,1) if (v_available_points == 22 && v_b2_ch2_deal != 3)
achievement("Who needs stats?",v_ac_b2_ch4_stats)
#if(v_b2_ch4_charge == 3 && v_b2_ch2_lessathi != 0 || v_b2_ch4_charge == 3 && v_b2_ch2_threatened != 2) {
 "Where's Wilhelm?" Bruce asks, looking around the sand. "Wasn't he with you?"

"Over there," I say, nodding toward Wilhelm's motionless form. "Claimed he was exhausted and took a nap."

"Wait, you dropped him?" Bruce asks. "He made a move on you?"

"Lucky guess," I say.

"Told you he was an assassin," Bruce grunts. "Never trust a snake. I've been watching my back since we entered the arena. Napping is fine, but the next division is staging at the gates. I'll get him up."

Bruce strides over to Wilhelm and lands three sharp slaps across his cheeks, shouting into his ear.

"Wilhelm! Up on your feet, you useless blade! Our first round is over. We need to clear the area."

Wilhelm's eyes snap open. His hand shoots out, clamping onto Bruce's wrist in a white-knuckled grip, murder burning behind his stare.

"I'm awake," Wilhelm says, forcing a calm tone in his voice. "Let's get out of here."

We make the long walk back to the division quarters. The moment the iron gate clangs shut behind us, Wilhelm heads for the side door.

"I need to go get something from my backpack," Wilhelm tells us, shortly after we enter the room. "I'll be right back."

"I hope you won't try to assassinate anyone else on your way to the locker room, Wilhelm," Bruce says. "If you get knocked out again, I'm not coming to wake you up."

Wilhelm gives Bruce a scornful look before he opens the door, but he leaves the room without saying another word.

"Attention, please," the announcer's voice echoes from the ceiling. "It appears that we need to take a small break, in order to do a little inventory of our remaining creatures. Please remain patient! This shouldn't take long!"

"Hah!" Bruce says. "They're already running out of creatures. I bet they weren't expecting so many of them to be taken out in the first few fights!"

}
#if(v_b2_ch2_lessathi != 0 && v_b2_ch4_charge != 3 || v_b2_ch2_threatened != 2 && v_b2_ch4_charge != 3) {
